\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Mean response length by condition and model (left axis, bars) overlaid with the Pearson correlation between per-example response-length gain and accuracy gain (right axis, diamonds). llama-3.1-8b-instruct's checksum-critique responses are roughly 8x longer than its baseline, and unlike the other two models, longer checksum responses are associated with worse accuracy for this model.}}{9}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fig3}{{3}{9}{Mean response length by condition and model (left axis, bars) overlaid with the Pearson correlation between per-example response-length gain and accuracy gain (right axis, diamonds). llama-3.1-8b-instruct's checksum-critique responses are roughly 8x longer than its baseline, and unlike the other two models, longer checksum responses are associated with worse accuracy for this model}{figure.3}{}}
